# /mode jev-on with a generator key configured (a fake OPENROUTER_API_KEY serves Jev and the generator): the mode item
# `mode jev+llm from the next run — …` and the badge `jev+llm · next run` in the console's top edge (TUI-DESIGN-2 §1.3,
# §1.5, H-G1, §8.2 mode-switch)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
sleep 0.2
send /mode jev-on
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect jev\+llm from the next run
expect ╭─ (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*jev\+llm(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* · next run
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
